% lps-converted-from: penalty.lps
% This document was written from the LPS program penalty.lps, which says the same thing in the older syntax. The two run alike, and tools/lps_to_le_test.pl checks that they do. The first line above is what keeps the older file from being read as this document's companion, which would run every rule twice.

the target language is: lps.

the maximum time is 6.

the events are:
    *a thing* emergenies occurs; known as emergency_occurs.
    *a thing* presss; known as press.

the actions are:
    *a thing* fines *a second thing*; known as fine.
    *a thing* warns; known as warn.

the fluents are:
    the emergency is *a thing*; known as emergency.
    *a thing* is fined *a second thing*; known as fined.

the templates are:
    the offender is *a thing*; known as offender.

the knowledge base penalty includes:

when a thing emergenies occurs
then the emergency is the thing.

when a thing fines a second thing
then the thing is fined the second thing.

if a thing presss to a time
    and it is not the case that the emergency is a second thing at the time
then the thing fines 50 from the time.

it must not be true that
    a thing is fined a second thing
    and it is not the case that the offender is the thing.

the offender is vandal.


scenario one is:
    vandal presss from 2 to 3.
